  "details": "Currently all variables need to be defined at the beginning of assembly, this creates many issues and mess when trying to implement normal support for methods, especially when trying to add recursion in some sane way, as simulating stack on this heap is pretty nasty.\nSo would be great to get support for stack memory with bytecodes to load/store variable probably with some way to define size of stack for event/method.\nLike this: \n```\n.code_start\n    \n// simillar to externs, _<name>__<arguments>__<returnType>\n_addInts__SystemInt_SystemInt__SystemInt:\n    .stackSize 3\n    loadInt 0 // first argument \n    loadInt 1 // second argument \n    extern natveAdd\n    returnInt\n// and calling them\n_update:\n    .stackSize 2\n    storeInt 0 3 // store 3 at index 0\n    storeInt 1 6\n    call _addInts__SystemInt_SystemInt__SystemInt\n    // now there is 9 at index 0\n```\ngist: https://gist.github.com/1504602ba979c8fd02749ed8c1f81f80\nAnd this would be even better with support for custom structures (that can be implemented just as some custom object that stores type name and map of parameters)\n\nThis would help a lot with creation of custom compilers and making the resulting code being fast.  Currently we are really limited to create anything that would allow to create more complex scripts.",
